---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PERSON_ID } from '../../lib/schema';

const advisory = {
	'@type': 'Service',
	'@id': 'https://okarthur.com/work/#advisory',
	name: 'Continuing advisory',
	serviceType:
		'Independent advisory on digital, data and AI in infrastructure',
	description:
		'Retained independent advice to infrastructure owners and leadership teams on digital, data and AI decisions and procurements, bought as a retainer or a defined block of days.',
	url: 'https://okarthur.com/work/',
	provider: { '@id': PERSON_ID },
	areaServed: [
		{ '@type': 'Country', name: 'United Arab Emirates' },
		{ '@type': 'Country', name: 'United Kingdom' },
		{ '@type': 'Place', name: 'Gulf Cooperation Council' },
	],
	audience: {
		'@type': 'Audience',
		audienceType:
			'Infrastructure owners, developers and major capital programmes',
	},
};
---

<Base
	title="Advisory, review and board work"
	description="Independent judgement from Steven Yule on an infrastructure decision before it is confirmed. A written review, continuing advisory or a board appointment."
	schema={[advisory]}
>
	<div class="page-head">
		<h1 class="page-title">Work</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			Three ways to commission independent judgement on a decision.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="prose numbered">
		<p>
			The three differ in how long the advice is needed. A single decision
			suits a review, which ends in a written opinion. Decisions that keep
			coming over months suit a retained adviser. Decisions taken by a board
			suit a non-executive appointment.
		</p>

		<h2 id="review">Independent review</h2>
		<p>
			A review gives a second opinion on one decision before it is confirmed.
			It might be a supplier's proposal or a business case. It might also be a
			change of plan at group level that affects several developments. Scope
			and end date are agreed before work starts. I propose a fixed fee after
			a first call. The output is one written opinion, short enough to put in
			front of a board and specific enough to act on.
		</p>
		<p>
			The <a href="/review/">review page</a> sets out what a review covers and
			what it does not.
		</p>

		<h2 id="advisory">Continuing advisory</h2>
		<p>
			Some decisions do not resolve in one opinion. When an owner needs
			independent advice over several months, I work as a retained adviser.
			It typically covers client-side support while a supplier delivers, or
			setting the scope and scoring of a procurement before it goes to market.
			It can also cover testing a digital or data strategy before it is
			funded.
		</p>
		<p>
			Advisory is bought as a retainer or a block of days agreed in advance.
			The independence rule that governs a review applies here too. I take no
			delivery or supplier-side work on anything I advise on. Any interest is
			declared before the engagement starts.
		</p>

		<h2 id="board">Board and non-executive</h2>
		<p>
			Boards are asked to approve digital and AI investment at a scale most of
			them cannot test. They are also asked to hold a portfolio of developments
			to its plan using reports written one development at a time. A board
			asked to approve a data platform usually sees a business case written by
			the people who will deliver it. Few members are in a position to
			question its assumptions.
		</p>
		<p>
			I take non-executive and advisory board appointments where that gap
			exists, with private companies in the UK and the UAE. I am a
			non-executive director of Thomas Telford Ltd. My career has been on the
			digital side of capital delivery, which is where most of these business
			cases come from.
		</p>

		<h2 id="speaking">Speaking and writing</h2>
		<p>
			I speak and write on digital, data and AI in infrastructure. I am also
			available for press comment. Recent talks and articles are listed under <a
				href="/elsewhere/">Published elsewhere</a
			>. The <a href="/media/">media page</a> has a biography and a photo for
			organisers and editors.
		</p>

		<h2 id="start-here">Start here</h2>
		<p>
			<a href="/contact/">Tell me the decision you are facing</a>, or the
			appointment you are trying to fill.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>
